Yes, by all means, I love discussions. In my opinion, to have information
material in other languages would serve only to give a more international
image, but it would have little practical use. I very much doubt that anyone
who doesn't already speak English would consider learning Lojban at this
point, and anyway, it's not much use having brochures if to learn the
vocabulary you need to understand English.

It would have been nice to have the list defining gismu in more than one
language, so that the meanings were not too attached to particular English
words, but I don't think that is much of a problem. I think that the first
things to translate should be the gismu and cmavo lists.

